    "content": "# Clinical / Block Program Knowledge Index\n\n> **Internal status \u2014 M1-WIKI-08 QA pass completed 2026-07-09**  \n> Internal index and working draft only. It does **not** make any listed clinical, legal, coding, reimbursement, documentation, or outcome material final. Every import defaults to internal, unapproved, review-gated, and client-inaccessible.\n\n## Overview\n\nThe Clinical / Block Program Knowledge Index maps Block Ops\u2019 clinical and implementation knowledge so the team can inventory, review, version, and promote materials without confusing source content with approved truth.\n\nThe foundation deliverables are the universal baseline inventory for every client. Universal inclusion does not waive clinical fact review, lawyer review, site-policy validation, coding/compliance review, evidence review, customization, or version control.\n\n## Status layers\n\n- source/imported material\n- internal draft or working material\n- review-needed material\n- reviewed internal operational truth\n- approved-final client content\n- client-visible or approved-agent content\n- superseded/archive material\n\nImporting, indexing, assigning, or rendering content never changes its status.\n\n## Knowledge groups\n\n### Physical Operations\n\n- Block Cart Par Level Guide\n- Block Cart Planogram\n- Block Bay Workflow Logic\n- Daily Cart Restock Checklist\n- Machine Cleaning Checklist\n- Probe Cover / Gel Management Standard\n- Clean vs Sterile Protocol\n\n### Human Capital and Training\n\n- Block Lead Nurse Responsibility List\n- Block Champion Charter\n- LAST Second Responder Nursing Competency\n- Sterile Setup Assist Competency\n\n### Patient and Stakeholder Integration\n\n- Nerve Block Patient Brochure\n- Post-Block Sensory Guide\n- Patient Red Flag Card\n- Fall Prevention Patient Agreement\n- Red Flag Recognition Card\n\n### Clinical Safety and Protocol Reference\n\n- Regional-anesthesia consent form\n- Local anesthetic systemic toxicity (LAST) protocol suite\n- High-volume dilution chart\n- Weight-based maximum-dose calculator\n- Standardized test-dose protocol\n- Block time-out checklist\n- Local-anesthetic selection algorithm\n- Adjuvant dosing guide\n- Intraneural-injection stop criteria\n- Hydrodissection opening-pressure protocol\n- Medication-specific utilization criteria\n\n### Documentation, EMR, and Value Intelligence\n\n- Block procedure note template\n- Post-anesthesia care unit block-assessment template\n- Preoperative nursing template\n- Block success/failure log\n- Block status-tracking guide\n- Morphine milligram equivalent calculator reference\n- Post-anesthesia care unit length-of-stay tracker\n- Medical-necessity phrases\n- Current Procedural Terminology / ICD-10 crosswalk\n\n### Ultrasound and Technique\n\n- In-plane technique SOP\n- Out-of-plane technique SOP\n- Triangle of Success setup guide\n- PART maneuver guide\n- Knobology cheat sheet\n\n## Required review gates\n\n### Qualified clinical fact review\n\nClinical facts and safety-, dosing-, technique-, protocol-, training-, and outcome-related content require documented qualified clinical fact review before being marked current, used by a client-facing agent, or released externally.\n\n### Lawyer approval\n\nLegal documents, consent forms, patient agreements, legal disclaimers, contract language, and legal/scope representations require lawyer approval before external use.\n\n### Coding, reimbursement, evidence, and site review\n\n- coding and reimbursement references require qualified billing/compliance review\n- outcome, ROI, and value claims require cited evidence and claim review\n- clinical documentation templates require qualified clinical and site-policy review, plus lawyer review where legal representations are involved\n- site-specific configuration requires accountable site-owner validation\n- client portal, search, download, and agent visibility requires Max verification against the live product\n\n## Promotion path\n\n1. Import as internal, unapproved, and client-inaccessible.\n2. Record stable source/repository identifiers and preserve source evidence.\n3. Assign a knowledge group, owner, audience, risk class, and intended use.\n4. Record version, effective date, currentness, and superseded state.\n5. Complete every applicable review gate.\n6. Distinguish reviewed internal operational truth from approved-final client content.\n7. Promote approved-final content only to the explicitly authorized client surfaces.\n8. Verify client visibility across portal pages, search, agents, downloads, cached links, and print packages.\n9. Archive superseded copies without deleting source evidence.\n\n## Deliverable-level review register\n\nEach item should record:\n\n- title and stable source identifier\n- owner and intended audience\n- risk class and client-visible flag\n- version, effective date, and superseded state\n- qualified clinical reviewer and decision where applicable\n- lawyer reviewer and decision where applicable\n- coding/compliance reviewer where applicable\n- site validation where applicable\n- evidence/claim review where applicable\n- approval date, expiration, and re-review trigger\n\n## Milestone application\n\n- **M3 \u2014 External validation:** attending reviewers test high-risk clinical and implementation knowledge.\n- **M4 \u2014 Foundational client completion:** approved materials support completion of the foundational client.\n- **M5 \u2014 Paid client onboarding:** approved-final materials support a paid client without exposing draft or unreviewed content.\n\n## Related Mission Control workflows/tasks\n\n- M1-WIKI-08 \u2014 QA Delivery and Clinical Knowledge Wiki pages\n- Clinical Standard and Deliverables\n- Deliverables and Content\n- Training and Support\n- QA and Validation\n- Security and Compliance\n- M4 Foundational Client Completion\n\n## Related wiki pages\n\n- [[Implementation Bundles]]\n- [[Implementation Bundle Delivery]]\n- [[Training Day Readiness]]\n- [[Go-Live Verification]]\n- [[Status Rules]]\n- [[Supabase Data Model]]\n\n## Open questions / needs update\n\n- Build the detailed deliverable-by-deliverable review register.\n- Confirm which documents have verifiable final markings and approval records.\n- Identify the exact qualified reviewers required for each risk class.\n- Replace machine-specific source paths with stable vault/repository identifiers.\n\n### QA note 2026-07-09\n\nThis pass establishes explicit status layers, qualified clinical and lawyer gates, a deliverable-level review schema, finals-only client visibility, and current M3/M4/M5 milestone application. The page remains internal and review-gated.\n",
    "kind": "wiki-page"
